IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg10-sos-service`
IMPORT `dg10-suits`
IMPORT `dg10-close-status`
IMPORT `dg10-close-governance`
IMPORT `dg10-pbc`
IMPORT `dg10-foreign-qualification`
IMPORT `dg10-foreign-withdrawal-and-suits`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapters XIII to XVI (ss 321-385) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, src:1632-1934, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online (not the
-- official text).
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation
-- Law: an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder. They ask what the Law
-- lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
-- Subchapter XVI is about corporations organized elsewhere; there the person is read as a director, officer,
-- incorporator or stockholder of the foreign corporation concerned, or its agent, or someone who deals with it.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person
-- would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the records the modules expect
-- from plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list), in its WHERE, and calls the module's rule. A
-- record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so. Where the
-- Law is silent on a case the answer is a MAYBE whose NOTHING means "the Law does not answer this here".
--
-- Where the existing encoding departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded in NOTES.md):
--   * Judgments the Law hands to someone else are taken as plain facts the person states ("the Court of Chancery
--     has approved ...", "the Court determines that ..."): s 322, s 324(c), s 348(b), s 352, s 353.
--   * The figures that other sections or other statutes fix (the fee under s 391(a)(29), the Securities Acts, the
--     Title 5 banking statutes, Title 6 s 8-112) are plain inputs, because those texts are not among the inputs.
--   * Provisions addressed only to an official (the Secretary of State's letter, the Attorney General's duty, the
--     Court of Chancery's power) are asked as what they mean to the person: what they are owed or exposed to.
--
-- Groups that arise only in a situation the person may not be in are marked in the heading's comment so that the
-- form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

§ `Delaware General Corporation Law, Subchapters XIII to XVI: the questions of a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock`

§§ `Suits against my corporation, its directors, officers or stockholders (s 321 to s 330)`

-- Situation: only if someone is suing, serving or attaching the stock of your corporation, or you are suing it.

DECLARE `Route of service on the Secretary of State` IS ONE OF
    `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)`
    `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)`
    `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)`
    `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)`

-- s 321. Service of process on a corporation: personally on an officer, director or the registered agent, by a copy
-- left at an abode, the registered office or another place of business (with conditions), on the Secretary of State
-- when the server cannot serve otherwise, or as another statute or rule of court allows.
@export Has process been validly served on my corporation (s 321)?
GIVEN `how the process was served` IS A `s 321(a) Way of serving process on the corporation` @desc How was the process served on the corporation? Choose the way that matches what was done.
      `the date the copy was handed over or left` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy delivered or left? (Give the date of delivery even if it was handed over personally.)
      `the return date written on the process` IS A DATE @desc What is the return date of the process?
      `a copy was left in the presence of an adult person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a copy was left at a home or place of business, was it left in the presence of an adult person? (No if it was handed over personally.)
      `the officer serving the process stated the manner of service in the return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer serving the process distinctly state the manner of service in the return?
      `the process is returnable forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the process returnable forthwith?
      `the server could not by due diligence serve the process in any way s 321(a) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the server, after due diligence, find that the process could not be served in any of the ways described above?
      `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the process was served on the Secretary of State, was that done by electronic transmission?
      `the Secretary of State has prescribed that way of electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State prescribed that way of serving process by electronic transmission?
      `the service was made under s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the service made in accordance with section 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has process been validly served on my corporation` IF
    `s 321 service of process on the corporation is effective` `my service` `the server could not by due diligence serve the process in any way s 321(a) allows` `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the Secretary of State has prescribed that way of electronic service` `the service was made under s 3111 of Title 10 or another statute or rule of court`
    WHERE
        `my service` MEANS `s 321(a) Service of process` WITH
            `the way the process was served` IS `how the process was served`
            `the date the copy was left` IS `the date the copy was handed over or left`
            `the return date of the process` IS `the return date written on the process`
            `the copy was left in the presence of an adult person` IS `a copy was left in the presence of an adult person`
            `the officer serving the process distinctly stated the manner of service in the return` IS `the officer serving the process stated the manner of service in the return`
            `the process is returnable forthwith` IS `the process is returnable forthwith`

-- s 321(b), s 376(b), s 381(d), s 382(c). After service on the Secretary of State, the Secretary of State must
-- notify the corporation by letter, to the address the route calls for, by mail or courier with proof of
-- delivery, enclosing the process.
@export Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires (ss 321(b), 376(b), 381(d), 382(c))?
GIVEN route IS A `Route of service on the Secretary of State` @desc By which route was the process served on the Secretary of State?
      `the Secretary of State sent the letter forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State send the letter forthwith?
      `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing and a signed record of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that records the mailing or deposit and records delivery by the recipient's signature?
      `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
      `an address for the principal place of business appears in the records the route relies on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Delaware or a qualified foreign corporation: does an address for the corporation's principal place of business appear on the Secretary of State's records (Delaware corporation) or on the last annual report (qualified foreign corporation)?
      `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter directed to that principal place of business?
      `the letter was directed to the last registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter directed to the corporation's last registered office?
      `the letter was directed to the address stated in the certificate of withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a foreign corporation that withdrew: was the letter directed to the address stated in the certificate it filed on withdrawing?
      `the letter was directed to the address the plaintiff furnished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a foreign corporation that never qualified: was the letter directed to the address the plaintiff furnished to the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` IF
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)` THEN `s 321(b) the Secretary of State's letter meets the section` `the letter` (`s 321(b) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `an address for the principal place of business appears in the records the route relies on` `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` `the letter was directed to the last registered office`)
    WHEN `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)` THEN `s 376(b) the Secretary of State's letter meets the subsection` `the letter` (`s 376(b) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `an address for the principal place of business appears in the records the route relies on` `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` `the letter was directed to the last registered office`)
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)` THEN `s 381(d) the Secretary of State's letter meets the subsection` `the letter` (`s 381(d) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `the letter was directed to the address stated in the certificate of withdrawal`)
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)` THEN `s 382(c) the Secretary of State's letter meets the subsection` `the letter` (`s 382(c) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `the letter was directed to the address the plaintiff furnished`)
    WHERE
        `the letter` MEANS `s 321(b) Letter from the Secretary of State` WITH
            `the Secretary of State sent the letter forthwith` IS `the Secretary of State sent the letter forthwith`
            `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit and a record of delivery signed` IS `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing and a signed record of delivery`
            `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State` IS `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served`

-- s 321(b), s 376(b), s 381(d), s 382(c). The plaintiff's duty when serving through the Secretary of State: serve
-- the process and papers in duplicate, notify the Secretary of State, and pay the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29).
@export As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State (ss 321(b), 376(b), 381(d), 382(c))?
GIVEN route IS A `Route of service on the Secretary of State` @desc By which route did you serve the Secretary of State?
      `I served the process and any other papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service was being effected that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service was being effected through the Secretary of State?
      `the amount I paid the Secretary of State` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay the Secretary of State for the use of the State, in dollars?
      `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29), in dollars? (That section is not among the rules here, so the figure is supplied.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` IF
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)` THEN `s 321(b) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` `my steps` `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`
    WHEN `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)` THEN `s 376(b) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` `my steps` `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)` THEN `s 381(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` `my steps` `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)` THEN `s 382(c) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` `my steps` `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`
    WHERE
        `my steps` MEANS `s 321(b) Plaintiff's steps` WITH
            `the plaintiff served the process and any other papers in duplicate` IS `I served the process and any other papers in duplicate`
            `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service was being effected so` IS `I notified the Secretary of State that service was being effected that way`
            `the amount the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State for the use of the State` IS `the amount I paid the Secretary of State`

@export If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs (ss 321(b), 376(b), 381(d), 382(c))?
GIVEN route IS A `Route of service on the Secretary of State` @desc By which route did you serve the Secretary of State?
      `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` IF
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)` THEN `s 321(b) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `I prevail in the proceeding`
    WHEN `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)` THEN `s 376(b) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `I prevail in the proceeding`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)` THEN `s 381(d) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `I prevail in the proceeding`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)` THEN `s 382(c) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `I prevail in the proceeding`

@export Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation (ss 321(b), 376(b), 381(d), 382(c))?
GIVEN route IS A `Route of service on the Secretary of State` @desc By which route was the process served on the Secretary of State?
      `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date do you want to know whether the record must still be kept?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` IF
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)` THEN `s 321(b) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date I am asking about`
    WHEN `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)` THEN `s 376(b) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date I am asking about`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)` THEN `s 381(d) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date I am asking about`
    WHEN `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)` THEN `s 382(c) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date I am asking about`

-- s 322. Refusing to obey a court order is a sufficient ground for the Court of Chancery to appoint a receiver; of a
-- foreign corporation, a receiver of its assets within this State.
@export Can the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for my corporation because it did not obey a court order (s 322)?
GIVEN `my corporation refused, failed or neglected to obey an order or decree of a court of this State within the time the court fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation refuse, fail or neglect to obey an order or decree of a court of Delaware within the time the court fixed?
      `where my corporation is organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is the corporation organized: Delaware, another US jurisdiction, or a jurisdiction outside the United States?
GIVETH A `s 322 Receiver that the Court of Chancery may appoint`
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for my corporation because it did not obey a court order` IS
    `s 322 the receiver for which the failure to obey is a sufficient ground` `my corporation refused, failed or neglected to obey an order or decree of a court of this State within the time the court fixed` `where my corporation is organized`

-- s 323. A party in interest may file a statement with the Attorney General after 30 days' disobedience of a peremptory
-- writ of mandamus; the Attorney General must then bring quo warranto; on proof the court decrees the charter forfeited.
@export As a party in interest, may I file a statement with the Attorney General because the corporation ignored a writ of mandamus (s 323)?
GIVEN `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the peremptory writ of mandamus was served on the corporation without the corporation obeying it?
      `I am a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ of mandamus issued?
      `the statement was prepared by me or my attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement of the failure prepared by you or your attorney?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a party in interest, may I file a statement with the Attorney General because the corporation ignored a writ of mandamus` IF
    `s 323 the party in interest may file a statement with the Attorney General` `the failure`
    WHERE
        `the failure` MEANS `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus` WITH
            `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on the corporation` IS `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on it`
            `the person is a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued` IS `I am a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued`
            `the statement of the failure was prepared by that party or that party's attorney` IS `the statement was prepared by me or my attorney`
            -- Placeholders: this rule does not read the next two fields.
            `the statement has been filed with the Attorney General` IS FALSE
            `the court has competent proof of the failure and proper proceedings have been had in quo warranto` IS FALSE

@export Can the court decree my corporation's charter forfeited because it ignored a writ of mandamus (s 323)?
GIVEN `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the peremptory writ of mandamus was served on the corporation without the corporation obeying it?
      `a party in interest in the proceeding filed a statement prepared by that party or that party's attorney with the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a party in interest in the proceeding file a statement of the failure, prepared by that party or that party's attorney, with the Attorney General?
      `the court has competent proof and proper quo warranto proceedings have been had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have competent proof of the failure, and have proper quo warranto proceedings been had?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court decree my corporation's charter forfeited because it ignored a writ of mandamus` IF
    `s 323 the court must decree the charter of the corporation forfeited` `the failure`
    WHERE
        `the failure` MEANS `s 323 Failure to obey a peremptory writ of mandamus` WITH
            `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on the corporation` IS `the number of days the corporation has failed to obey the writ since it was served on it`
            -- The statement is by a party in interest and is prepared by that party or the party's attorney in the case asked about.
            `the person is a party in interest in the proceeding in which the writ issued` IS `a party in interest in the proceeding filed a statement prepared by that party or that party's attorney with the Attorney General`
            `the statement of the failure was prepared by that party or that party's attorney` IS `a party in interest in the proceeding filed a statement prepared by that party or that party's attorney with the Attorney General`
            `the statement has been filed with the Attorney General` IS `a party in interest in the proceeding filed a statement prepared by that party or that party's attorney with the Attorney General`
            `the court has competent proof of the failure and proper proceedings have been had in quo warranto` IS `the court has competent proof and proper quo warranto proceedings have been had`

-- s 324(a). My shares, option, right or interest may be attached for my debt if I appear on the books as holder
-- and, unless uncertificated, s 8-112 of Title 6 is satisfied.
@export Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt (s 324(a))?
GIVEN `the attachment is for a debt or other demand against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the attachment for a debt or other demand against you?
      `I appear on the books of the corporation to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear on the corporation's books to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest?
      `my interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest an uncertificated security (a security with no certificate), as defined in section 8-102 of Title 6?
      `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 8-112 of Title 6 (the rule on levies on certificated securities) been satisfied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` IF
        `s 324(a) the shares, option, right or interest may be attached` `the attachment is for a debt or other demand against me` `I appear on the books of the corporation to hold or own the shares, option, right or interest`
    AND `s 324(a) the attachment may be laid` `my interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied`

@export Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now (s 324(a))?
GIVEN `my interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest an uncertificated security (a security with no certificate), as defined in section 8-102 of Title 6?
      `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 8-112 of Title 6 been satisfied?
      `final judgment has been rendered in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has final judgment been rendered in the case?
      `notice has been given as is required for sales upon execution process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of the sale been given as the law requires for sales upon execution process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now` IF
    `s 324(a) an order of sale may issue` `my interest is an uncertificated security as defined in s 8-102 of Title 6` `s 8-112 of Title 6 has been satisfied` `final judgment has been rendered in the case` `notice has been given as is required for sales upon execution process`

@export Has enough of my shares been sold to cover the debt, interest and costs, so that no more may be sold (s 324(a))?
GIVEN `the amount of the debt or other demand` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the debt or other demand, in dollars?
      `the interest on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest is owed on it, in dollars?
      `the costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the costs, in dollars?
      `the proceeds of the sale so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has the sale produced so far, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has enough of my shares been sold to cover the debt, interest and costs, so that no more may be sold` IF
    `s 324(a) the part already sold is sufficient to satisfy the debt, interest and costs` `the amount of the debt or other demand` `the interest on it` `the costs` `the proceeds of the sale so far`

@export Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient (s 324(a))?
GIVEN `I live out of the county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live out of the county in which the attachment process issued?
      `I am a nonresident of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a nonresident of Delaware?
      `a copy of the order was sent to my last known address by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order sent to your last known address by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested?
      `a newspaper is published in the county of my last known residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a newspaper published in the county of your last known residence?
      `the order was published in a newspaper in the county of my last known residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order published in a newspaper published in the county of your last known residence?
      `the number of times the order was published` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times was the order published?
      `the number of successive weeks over which it was published` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many successive weeks was it published?
      `the order was published in a newspaper in the county where the attachment process issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order published in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued?
      `the number of days from the last publication to the sale` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the sale did the last publication appear?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` IF
    `s 324(a) the notice of the sale by mail and publication is sufficient` `the notice`
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS `s 324(a) Notice of the sale` WITH
            `the debtor lives out of the county` IS `I live out of the county`
            `the debtor is a nonresident of this State` IS `I am a nonresident of Delaware`
            `a copy of the order was sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, to the debtor's last known address` IS `a copy of the order was sent to my last known address by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested`
            `a newspaper is published in the county of the debtor's last known residence` IS `a newspaper is published in the county of my last known residence`
            `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county of the debtor's last known residence` IS `the order was published in a newspaper in the county of my last known residence`
            `the number of times the order was published` IS `the number of times the order was published`
            `the number of successive weeks over which the order was published` IS `the number of successive weeks over which it was published`
            `the order was published in a newspaper published in the county where the attachment process issued` IS `the order was published in a newspaper in the county where the attachment process issued`
            `the number of days from the last publication to the sale` IS `the number of days from the last publication to the sale`

@export Is my transfer of the shares void because it was made after attachment and the shares were sold (s 324(a))?
GIVEN `the shares, option, right or interest have been sold under s 324` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the attached shares, option, right or interest been sold?
      `I assigned or transferred them after the attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assign or transfer them after the attachment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my transfer of the shares void because it was made after attachment and the shares were sold` IF
    `s 324(a) the debtor's assignment or transfer after attachment is void` `the shares, option, right or interest have been sold under s 324` `I assigned or transferred them after the attachment`

-- s 324(b). The attachment process is served on the corporation; the corporation must within 20 days serve a
-- certificate on the plaintiff, whatever its certificate of incorporation or bylaws say.
@export By what date must my corporation serve its certificate of the debtor's shares on the plaintiff (s 324(b))?
GIVEN `the date the attachment process was served on the corporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the attachment process served on the corporation?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my corporation serve its certificate of the debtor's shares on the plaintiff` IS
    `s 324(b) the last day for the corporation to serve the certificate on the plaintiff` `the date the attachment process was served on the corporation`

@export Has my corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff in time and with what is required (s 324(b))?
GIVEN `the date the attachment process was served on the corporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the attachment process served on the corporation?
      `the date the corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation serve its certificate on the plaintiff?
      `the debtor appears on our books to hold shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the debtor appear on the corporation's books to hold or own shares?
      `the certificate gives the number of shares with the numbers or marks distinguishing them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate give the number of shares, with the number or other marks distinguishing them?
      `the debtor appears on our books to have an option, right or interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the debtor appear on the corporation's books to have an option, right or interest in shares?
      `the certificate sets that option, right or interest forth in the language and form of our books` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set out that option, right or interest in the language and form in which it appears on the books?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff in time and with what is required` IF
        `s 324(b) the corporation served the certificate in time` `the date the attachment process was served on the corporation` `the date the corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff`
    AND `s 324(b) the certificate states what the subsection requires` `the debtor appears on our books to hold shares` `the certificate gives the number of shares with the numbers or marks distinguishing them` `the debtor appears on our books to have an option, right or interest in shares` `the certificate sets that option, right or interest forth in the language and form of our books`

@export Can a provision of my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws excuse it from serving the certificate on the plaintiff (s 324(b))?
GIVEN `where the provision is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where does the provision that would excuse the corporation sit: the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a board resolution, or nowhere?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a provision of my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws excuse it from serving the certificate on the plaintiff` IF
    `s 324(b) a provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws relieves the corporation of the duty to serve the certificate` `where the provision is made`

-- s 324(c). What the purchaser at a confirmed sale takes.
@export Is the purchaser at the sale of my attached shares entitled to the shares, option, right or interest (s 324(c))?
GIVEN `the sale has been made and confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sale been made and confirmed?
      `a certified copy of the order of sale and return was left with an officer, a director or the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certified copy of the order of sale and return left with an officer or director or with the corporation's registered agent?
      `there is a stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a stock certificate for the shares?
      `the stock certificate was left with an officer, a director or the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the stock certificate left with an officer or director or with the registered agent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the purchaser at the sale of my attached shares entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` IF
    `s 324(c) the purchaser is entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` `the sale has been made and confirmed` `a certified copy of the order of sale and return was left with an officer, a director or the registered agent` `there is a stock certificate` `the stock certificate was left with an officer, a director or the registered agent`

@export Is the purchaser entitled to a dividend that was declared or became payable after the attachment (s 324(c))?
GIVEN `the purchaser is entitled to the shares under s 324(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purchaser entitled to the shares, option, right or interest?
      `the dividend was declared or became payable since the attachment was laid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the dividend or income declared or did it become payable since the attachment was laid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the purchaser entitled to a dividend that was declared or became payable after the attachment` IF
    `s 324(c) the purchaser is entitled to the income or dividend` `the purchaser is entitled to the shares under s 324(c)` `the dividend was declared or became payable since the attachment was laid`

@export Does the sale transfer my shares to the purchaser even though my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws restrict transfer (s 324(c))?
GIVEN `the sale has been returned and confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sale been returned and confirmed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the sale transfer my shares to the purchaser even though my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws restrict transfer` IF
    `s 324(c) the sale transfers the shares, option, right or interest to the purchaser despite any contrary provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` `the sale has been returned and confirmed`

@export Can the court make my corporation issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and cancel the registration of the attached shares (s 324(c))?
GIVEN `the court issued the levy and confirmed the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the court that issued the levy and confirmed the sale?
      `the purchaser has given an open end bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the purchaser given an open end bond?
      `the court finds the bond adequate to protect the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court find the bond adequate to protect the corporation? (That is the court's judgment; say yes only if it has so found.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make my corporation issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and cancel the registration of the attached shares` IF
    `s 324(c) the court has the power to order the corporation to issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and to cancel the registration` `the court issued the levy and confirmed the sale` `the purchaser has given an open end bond` `the court finds the bond adequate to protect the corporation`

@export Is the money from the sale of my shares applied as the law of attachment of personal property directs (s 324(d))?
GIVEN `the money arose from the sale of the shares or of the option, right or interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the money arise from the sale of the shares, option, right or interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the money from the sale of my shares applied as the law of attachment of personal property directs` IF
    `s 324(d) the money is applied and paid by the public official as the law of attachment of personal property directs` `the money arose from the sale of the shares or of the option, right or interest`

-- s 325. A person to whom officers, directors or stockholders are liable by this chapter for the corporation's debts
-- may sue them; but not until judgment against the corporation and execution returned unsatisfied.
@export Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation (s 325)?
GIVEN `I am an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation?
      `a provision of this chapter makes me liable to pay the debts of the corporation or a part of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the General Corporation Law make you liable to pay the corporation's debts, or part of them? (Say yes only if some provision of the Law does so.)
      `the creditor is a person to whom I am so liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the creditor a person to whom you are so liable?
      `judgment has been obtained against the corporation for the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the creditor obtained judgment against the corporation for the debt?
      `execution on that judgment has been returned unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has execution on that judgment been returned unsatisfied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` IF
        `s 325(a) the plaintiff may sue the defendant at law or in equity` `I am an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `a provision of this chapter makes me liable to pay the debts of the corporation or a part of them` `the creditor is a person to whom I am so liable`
    AND (CONSIDER `s 325(b) a suit may be brought against the officer, director or stockholder for the debt of the corporation` `I am an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `judgment has been obtained against the corporation for the debt` `execution on that judgment has been returned unsatisfied`
         WHEN JUST bar THEN bar
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

@export Does the complaint I file against officers, directors or stockholders state what the Law requires (s 325(a))?
GIVEN `the complaint states the claim against the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the complaint state the claim against the corporation?
      `the complaint states the ground on which I expect to charge the defendants personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the complaint state the ground on which you expect to charge the defendants personally?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the complaint I file against officers, directors or stockholders state what the Law requires` IF
    `s 325(a) the complaint states what the subsection requires` `the complaint states the claim against the corporation` `the complaint states the ground on which I expect to charge the defendants personally`

-- s 326. An officer, director or stockholder who pays a corporate debt the chapter makes them liable for may recover it
-- from the corporation, out of the corporation's property only.
@export Can I recover from the corporation a corporate debt that I paid (s 326)?
GIVEN `I am an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation?
      `I paid a debt of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay a debt of the corporation?
      `a provision of this chapter makes me liable for that debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the General Corporation Law make you liable for that debt?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I recover from the corporation a corporate debt that I paid` IF
    `s 326 the person may recover the amount paid from the corporation` `I am an officer, director or stockholder of the corporation` `I paid a debt of the corporation` `a provision of this chapter makes me liable for that debt`

@export How much can I recover from the corporation for a debt of the corporation that I paid (s 326)?
GIVEN `I may recover from the corporation under s 326` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to recover under section 326 (you are an officer, director or stockholder, and paid a corporate debt the Law makes you liable for)?
      `the amount I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can I recover from the corporation for a debt of the corporation that I paid` IS
    `s 326 the amount the person may recover` `I may recover from the corporation under s 326` `the amount I paid`

@export In my action against the corporation for a debt I paid, can this property be taken (s 326)?
GIVEN `the property belongs to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property belong to the corporation (not to a stockholder)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `In my action against the corporation for a debt I paid, can this property be taken` IF
    `s 326 the property is liable to be taken in the action` `the property belongs to the corporation`

-- s 327. A derivative complaint must aver that the plaintiff held the stock at the time of the transaction, or that
-- the stock later came to the plaintiff by operation of law.
@export In my derivative suit, can my complaint make the averment of stock ownership the Law requires (s 327)?
GIVEN `I was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction I complain of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction you complain of?
      `my stock thereafter came to me by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your stock come to you after that transaction by operation of law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `In my derivative suit, can my complaint make the averment of stock ownership the Law requires` IF
    `s 327 the complaint contains the averment of stock ownership that the section requires` `I was a stockholder of the corporation at the time of the transaction I complain of` `my stock thereafter came to me by operation of law`

-- s 328. A sale of assets, a change in capital stock, a merger or consolidation or an amendment of the certificate
-- does not lessen the liability of the corporation, its stockholders, directors or officers, or the remedies of creditors.
@export Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction (s 328)?
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a Delaware corporation?
      `the transaction` IS A `s 328 Event that does not lessen liability or remedies` @desc Which transaction is it: a sale of assets, an increase or a decrease in capital stock, a merger or consolidation, a change or amendment of the certificate of incorporation, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction` IS
    `s 328 the event lessens or impairs the liability or the rights or remedies` `the corporation is a corporation of this State` `the transaction`

-- s 329. No corporation of this State, and no person it sues, may assert want of legal organization as a defense; the
-- courts may still inquire into the regularity of its organization or its possession of a power.
@export Can this party assert that the corporation was not legally organized as a defense to a claim (s 329(a))?
GIVEN party IS A `s 329(a) Party who would assert want of legal organization` @desc Who would assert it: a corporation of Delaware, a person sued by a Delaware corporation, or another party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this party assert that the corporation was not legally organized as a defense to a claim` IS
    `s 329(a) the party is permitted to assert want of legal organization as a defense to a claim` party

@export Can a court inquire into the regularity of my corporation's organization or its possession of a power it asserts, and hear evidence on it (s 329(b))?
GIVEN `my corporation asserts its existence or a power in a suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation assert its corporate existence or a corporate power in a suit or proceeding?
      `that existence or power is challenged there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that corporate existence, or its power to exercise the corporate rights it asserts, challenged in that suit or proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a court inquire into the regularity of my corporation's organization or its possession of a power it asserts, and hear evidence on it` IF
        `s 329(b) judicial inquiry into the regularity or validity of the organization or the lawful possession of the power is not prevented` `my corporation asserts its existence or a power in a suit or proceeding` `that existence or power is challenged there`
    AND `s 329(b) evidence tending to sustain the challenge is admissible` `my corporation asserts its existence or a power in a suit or proceeding` `that existence or power is challenged there`

-- s 330. No corporation may plead a statute against usury in a suit to enforce its bond, note or other evidence of
-- indebtedness.
@export Can my corporation plead a usury statute against its own bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness (s 330)?
GIVEN `the suit is to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness the corporation issued or assumed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the suit to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness that the corporation issued or assumed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my corporation plead a usury statute against its own bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness` IS
    `s 330 the corporation may plead a statute against usury` `the suit is to enforce payment of a bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness the corporation issued or assumed`

§§ `My close corporation (s 341 to s 356)`

-- Situation: only if your corporation is, or is becoming, a close corporation (a corporation whose certificate limits
-- it to no more than 30 holders of record, restricts transfers and bars a public offering).

-- s 341. Which law governs.
@export Is the close corporation subchapter part of the law that governs my corporation (s 341)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a close corporation as defined in s 342` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation as s 342 defines it (formed under s 343 or electing under s 344)?
GIVETH A `s 341(a) Law that governs a corporation`
DECIDE `Is the close corporation subchapter part of the law that governs my corporation` IS
    `s 341(a) the law that governs the corporation` `my corporation is a close corporation as defined in s 342`

@export On this point, does the General Corporation Law apply to my close corporation (s 341(b))?
GIVEN `my corporation is a close corporation as defined in s 342` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation as s 342 defines it?
      `the close corporation subchapter otherwise provides on this point` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subchapter XIV (ss 341 to 356) provide something different on this point?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `On this point, does the General Corporation Law apply to my close corporation` IS
    `s 341(b) this chapter is applicable to the close corporation on the point` `my corporation is a close corporation as defined in s 342` `the close corporation subchapter otherwise provides on this point`

-- s 342(a). A close corporation is organized under the chapter, its certificate has the s 102 provisions, and it provides
-- (1) certificated stock held of record by not more than a specified number of persons (at most 30), (2) transfer
-- restrictions permitted by s 202, (3) no public offering.
@export Is my corporation a close corporation (s 342(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the General Corporation Law?
      `our certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by s 102` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain the provisions that s 102 requires?
      `our certificate says all issued stock is represented by certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say that all the issued stock of all classes, apart from treasury shares, is represented by certificates?
      `our certificate says the stock is held of record by no more than a specified number of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say that the issued stock is held of record by not more than a specified number of persons?
      `the number of persons our certificate specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of holders of record does the certificate specify?
      `our certificate subjects all issued stock to transfer restrictions permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate subject all the issued stock of all classes to one or more of the transfer restrictions that s 202 permits?
      `our certificate says there will be no public offering of our stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say the corporation will make no offering of its stock that would be a public offering under the Securities Act of 1933?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation a close corporation` IF
    `s 342(a) the corporation is a close corporation` `our certificate`
    WHERE
        `our certificate` MEANS `s 342(a) Certificate of incorporation of a corporation` WITH
            `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law`
            `the certificate contains the provisions required by s 102` IS `our certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by s 102`
            `the certificate provides that all the issued stock of all classes, exclusive of treasury shares, is represented by certificates` IS `our certificate says all issued stock is represented by certificates`
            `the certificate provides that the issued stock is held of record by not more than a specified number of persons` IS `our certificate says the stock is held of record by no more than a specified number of persons`
            `the number of persons the certificate specifies` IS `the number of persons our certificate specifies`
            `the certificate provides that all the issued stock of all classes is subject to 1 or more of the restrictions on transfer permitted by s 202` IS `our certificate subjects all issued stock to transfer restrictions permitted by s 202`
            `the certificate provides that the corporation will make no offering of its stock that would constitute a public offering within the meaning of the Securities Act of 1933` IS `our certificate says there will be no public offering of our stock`

-- s 342(b). The certificate may set the qualifications of stockholders.
@export Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock (s 342(b))?
GIVEN `the certificate lists classes of persons entitled to be holders of record of stock of this class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate list classes of persons who are entitled to be holders of record of stock of this class?
      `I am in one of those classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in one of those classes?
      `the certificate lists classes of persons not entitled to be holders of stock of this class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate list classes of persons who are not entitled to be holders of stock of this class?
      `I am in one of the classes not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in one of the classes that are not entitled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` IF
    `s 342(b) the person is entitled under the certificate to be a holder of record of the stock` `the certificate lists classes of persons entitled to be holders of record of stock of this class` `I am in one of those classes` `the certificate lists classes of persons not entitled to be holders of stock of this class` `I am in one of the classes not entitled`

-- s 342(c). Stock held in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties counts as held by one stockholder.
@export How many holders of record does my close corporation have, counting joint holdings as one (s 342(c))?
GIVEN `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than jointly` IS A NUMBER @desc How many holders of record hold stock otherwise than in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties?
      `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties holding stock of record` IS A NUMBER @desc How many joint or common tenancies, or tenancies by the entireties, hold stock of record? (Each counts as one stockholder.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many holders of record does my close corporation have, counting joint holdings as one` IS
    `s 342(c) the number of holders of record of the stock` `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than jointly` `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties holding stock of record`

@export Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows (s 342(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than jointly` IS A NUMBER @desc How many holders of record hold stock otherwise than in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties?
      `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties holding stock of record` IS A NUMBER @desc How many joint or common tenancies, or tenancies by the entireties, hold stock of record?
      `the number of persons our certificate specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of holders of record does the certificate specify?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows` IF
    `s 342(a)(1) the stock is held of record by more persons than the certificate specifies` (`s 342(c) the number of holders of record of the stock` `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than jointly` `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties holding stock of record`) `the number of persons our certificate specifies`

-- s 343. Formation of a close corporation.
@export Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires (s 343)?
GIVEN `we were formed in accordance with ss 101, 102 and 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the corporation formed in accordance with ss 101, 102 and 103?
      `our certificate has a heading stating our name and that we are a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain a heading stating the corporation's name and that it is a close corporation?
      `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the General Corporation Law?
      `our certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by s 102` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain the provisions that s 102 requires?
      `our certificate says all issued stock is represented by certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say that all the issued stock of all classes, apart from treasury shares, is represented by certificates?
      `our certificate says the stock is held of record by no more than a specified number of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say that the issued stock is held of record by not more than a specified number of persons?
      `the number of persons our certificate specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of holders of record does the certificate specify?
      `our certificate subjects all issued stock to transfer restrictions permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate subject all the issued stock of all classes to one or more of the transfer restrictions that s 202 permits?
      `our certificate says there will be no public offering of our stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say the corporation will make no offering of its stock that would be a public offering under the Securities Act of 1933?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires` IF
    `s 343 the close corporation is formed` `we were formed in accordance with ss 101, 102 and 103` `our certificate has a heading stating our name and that we are a close corporation` `our certificate`
    WHERE
        `our certificate` MEANS `s 342(a) Certificate of incorporation of a corporation` WITH
            `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law`
            `the certificate contains the provisions required by s 102` IS `our certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by s 102`
            `the certificate provides that all the issued stock of all classes, exclusive of treasury shares, is represented by certificates` IS `our certificate says all issued stock is represented by certificates`
            `the certificate provides that the issued stock is held of record by not more than a specified number of persons` IS `our certificate says the stock is held of record by no more than a specified number of persons`
            `the number of persons the certificate specifies` IS `the number of persons our certificate specifies`
            `the certificate provides that all the issued stock of all classes is subject to 1 or more of the restrictions on transfer permitted by s 202` IS `our certificate subjects all issued stock to transfer restrictions permitted by s 202`
            `the certificate provides that the corporation will make no offering of its stock that would constitute a public offering within the meaning of the Securities Act of 1933` IS `our certificate says there will be no public offering of our stock`

-- s 344. Election by an existing corporation. "Each class" is asked as the class whose holders approved the least:
-- if the least-approving class carries, every class does.
@export Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to (s 344)?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the General Corporation Law?
      `our certificate of amendment says we elect to become a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of amendment contain a statement that the corporation elects to become a close corporation?
      `our certificate of amendment contains the provisions s 342 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of amendment contain the provisions that s 342 requires in the certificate of a close corporation?
      `our certificate of amendment has the close corporation heading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of amendment contain a heading stating the corporation's name and that it is a close corporation?
      `our certificate of amendment was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of amendment executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103?
      `the amendment was adopted in accordance with s 241 or s 242` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amendment adopted in accordance with s 241 or s 242?
      `the shares of the class with the least approval that are outstanding` IS A NUMBER @desc Take the class of stock whose holders of record approved the least. How many of its shares are outstanding?
      `the shares of that class held by the holders of record who approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class are held of record by the holders who approved the election?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` IS
    `s 344 the corporation has become a close corporation by election` `our election` (LIST `the least approving class`)
    WHERE
        `our election` MEANS `s 344 Election to become a close corporation` WITH
            `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law`
            `the certificate of amendment contains a statement that the corporation elects to become a close corporation` IS `our certificate of amendment says we elect to become a close corporation`
            `the certificate of amendment contains the provisions required by s 342 to appear in the certificate of a close corporation` IS `our certificate of amendment contains the provisions s 342 requires`
            `the certificate of amendment contains a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation` IS `our certificate of amendment has the close corporation heading`
            `the certificate of amendment was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103` IS `our certificate of amendment was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103`
            `the amendment was adopted in accordance with the requirements of s 241 or s 242` IS `the amendment was adopted in accordance with s 241 or s 242`
        `the least approving class` MEANS `s 344 Class vote` WITH
            `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 344 vote` IS `the shares of the class with the least approval that are outstanding`
            `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 344 vote` IS `the shares of that class held by the holders of record who approved`

-- s 345. Continuation of close corporation status.
@export Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation (s 345)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation now?
      `we filed a certificate of amendment deleting the s 342 provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation filed with the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment deleting the provisions that s 342 requires or permits?
      `a condition in our certificate under s 342 has in fact been breached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any provision or condition required or permitted by s 342 in the certificate in fact been breached?
      `the corporation or a stockholder took the steps s 348 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation or any stockholder take the steps that s 348 requires to prevent the loss of status or to remedy the breach?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` IF
    `s 345 the corporation continues to be a close corporation` `my corporation is a close corporation` `we filed a certificate of amendment deleting the s 342 provisions` `a condition in our certificate under s 342 has in fact been breached` `the corporation or a stockholder took the steps s 348 requires`

-- s 346. Voluntary termination: 2/3 of each class, or the greater vote the certificate requires.
@export What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote (s 346)?
GIVEN `our certificate requires a greater vote of this class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation require, for terminating close corporation status, a vote greater than 2/3 or a vote of all the shares of this class?
      `the percentage of this class that it requires` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of the shares of this class does it require? (Enter 75 for 75%, and 100 for all the shares.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote` IS
    `s 346(b) the proportion of the class required to terminate close corporation status` (IF `our certificate requires a greater vote of this class` THEN JUST (`the percentage of this class that it requires` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING)

@export Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status (s 346(a))?
GIVEN `the amendment was adopted and became effective in accordance with s 242` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amendment adopted and did it become effective in accordance with s 242?
      `the shares of the class with the least approval that are outstanding` IS A NUMBER @desc Take the class of stock whose holders of record approved the least. How many of its shares are outstanding?
      `the shares of that class held by the holders of record who approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class are held of record by the holders who approved the amendment?
      `our certificate requires a greater vote of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate require, for that class, a vote greater than 2/3 or a vote of all its shares?
      `the percentage of that class that it requires` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of the shares of that class does it require? (Enter 75 for 75%, and 100 for all the shares.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` IS
    `s 346(a) the corporation has voluntarily terminated its close corporation status` (LIST `the least approving class`) `the amendment was adopted and became effective in accordance with s 242`
    WHERE
        `the least approving class` MEANS `s 346 Class vote` WITH
            `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 346 vote` IS `the shares of the class with the least approval that are outstanding`
            `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 346 vote` IS `the shares of that class held by the holders of record who approved`
            `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` IS (IF `our certificate requires a greater vote of that class` THEN JUST (`the percentage of that class that it requires` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 347. Stock issued or transferred in breach of the qualifying conditions.
@export As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I am not eligible to be a holder of this stock (s 347(a))?
GIVEN `I am not entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person who is not entitled under the certificate of incorporation (s 342(b)) to be a holder of record of this stock?
      `the stock certificate conspicuously notes who may be holders of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock certificate conspicuously note the qualifications of the persons entitled to be holders of record?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I am not eligible to be a holder of this stock` IF
    `s 347(a) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice of the transferee's ineligibility` `I am not entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record` `the stock certificate conspicuously notes who may be holders of record`

@export As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows (s 347(b))?
GIVEN `the certificate states a number of persons entitled to be holders of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation state a number of persons, not in excess of 30, who are entitled to be holders of record?
      `the number of persons the certificate states` IS A NUMBER @desc What number does it state?
      `the stock certificate conspicuously states that number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock certificate conspicuously state that number?
      `the number of persons who would hold the stock after the transfer` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons would hold the stock after the issuance or transfer to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` IF
    `s 347(b) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice that the stock would be held by more than the stated number of persons` `the certificate states a number of persons entitled to be holders of record` `the number of persons the certificate states` `the stock certificate conspicuously states that number` `the number of persons who would hold the stock after the transfer`

@export As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction (s 347(c))?
GIVEN `the stock certificate conspicuously notes a restriction on transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock certificate conspicuously note the fact of a restriction on transfer of the stock?
      `the restriction is one permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the restriction one that s 202 permits?
      `my acquisition violates the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your acquisition violate the restriction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction` IF
    `s 347(c) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice that the stock was acquired in violation of the restriction` `the stock certificate conspicuously notes a restriction on transfer` `the restriction is one permitted by s 202` `my acquisition violates the restriction`

@export May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name (s 347(d), (e))?
GIVEN `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that I am not eligible to hold the stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have notice, or are you presumed under s 347(a) to have notice, that you are not eligible to be a holder of the corporation's stock?
      `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that the transfer exceeds the permitted number of holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have notice, or are you presumed under s 347(b) to have notice, that the transfer would put the stock in more hands than the certificate permits?
      `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that the transfer breaks a transfer restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have notice, or are you presumed under s 347(c) to have notice, that the transfer is in violation of a restriction on transfer?
      `all the stockholders consented to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did all the stockholders of the close corporation consent to the transfer?
      `the corporation has amended its certificate in accordance with s 346` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with s 346 (ending its close corporation status)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` IF
    `s 347(d) the corporation may refuse to register the transfer of the stock into the name of the transferee` `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that I am not eligible to hold the stock` `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that the transfer exceeds the permitted number of holders` `I have, or am presumed to have, notice that the transfer breaks a transfer restriction` (`s 347(e) subsection (d) does not apply` `all the stockholders consented to the transfer` `the corporation has amended its certificate in accordance with s 346`)

@export Does section 347 cover a transfer of stock that was not for value, such as a gift (s 347(f))?
GIVEN `stock was issued or transferred, whether or not for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was stock of the close corporation issued or transferred to the person, whether or not for value?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 347 cover a transfer of stock that was not for value, such as a gift` IF
    `s 347(f) the issuance or transfer, whether or not for value, is a transfer for the purposes of s 347` `stock was issued or transferred, whether or not for value`

@export Does section 347 take away my right to rescind the transfer or to recover under a warranty (s 347(g))?
GIVEN `I have a right under other law to rescind or to recover under an express or implied warranty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right under other law to rescind the transaction, or to recover under an express or implied warranty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 347 take away my right to rescind the transfer or to recover under a warranty` IS
    `s 347(g) the section impairs the transferee's right to rescind the transaction or to recover under a warranty` `I have a right under other law to rescind or to recover under an express or implied warranty`

-- s 348. A breach ends close corporation status unless, within 30 days after the event or its discovery (whichever is
-- later), the corporation files a certificate and furnishes a copy to each stockholder, and concurrently corrects the
-- situation; the Court of Chancery may act on a suit by the corporation or a stockholder.
@export By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status (s 348(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the date the event occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the event occur that breached a condition of the close corporation's certificate?
      `the date the event was discovered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the event discovered?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status` IS
    `s 348(a)(1) the later of 30 days after the event and 30 days after its discovery` `the date the event occurred` `the date the event was discovered`

@export Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach (s 348(a))?
GIVEN `the date the event occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the event occur that breached a condition of the close corporation's certificate?
      `the date the event was discovered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the event discovered?
      `the date we filed the certificate with the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation file the certificate with the Secretary of State?
      `our certificate states that a specified provision or condition has ceased to be applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a specified provision or condition included under s 342 has ceased to be applicable?
      `our certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103?
      `we furnished a copy of the certificate to each stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation furnish a copy of the certificate to each stockholder?
      `we took the steps necessary to correct the situation when we filed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation, concurrently with the filing, take the steps necessary to correct the situation (for example, refusing to register a wrongful transfer, or starting a proceeding under s 348(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` IS
    `s 348(a) the corporation's status as a close corporation survives the breach` `our steps`
    WHERE
        `our steps` MEANS `s 348(a) Steps taken after a breach` WITH
            `the date the event occurred` IS `the date the event occurred`
            `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered` IS JUST `the date the event was discovered`
            `the date the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State` IS `the date we filed the certificate with the Secretary of State`
            `the certificate states that a specified provision or condition has ceased to be applicable` IS `our certificate states that a specified provision or condition has ceased to be applicable`
            `the certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS `our certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`
            `a copy of the certificate was furnished to each stockholder` IS `we furnished a copy of the certificate to each stockholder`
            `the corporation took the steps necessary to correct the situation on the date the certificate was filed` IS `we took the steps necessary to correct the situation when we filed the certificate`

@export Can I (or the corporation) ask the Court of Chancery for orders to prevent the loss of close corporation status (s 348(b))?
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the suit brought by the corporation or by a stockholder?
      `the act or threatened act is inconsistent with a condition required or permitted by s 342` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act, or threatened act, of the corporation or a stockholder inconsistent with a provision or condition that s 342 requires or permits in the certificate?
      `the act was approved in accordance with s 346` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act approved in accordance with s 346?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I (or the corporation) ask the Court of Chancery for orders to prevent the loss of close corporation status` IF
    `s 348(b) the Court of Chancery has jurisdiction to issue orders to prevent loss of close corporation status or to restore it` `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` `the act or threatened act is inconsistent with a condition required or permitted by s 342` `the act was approved in accordance with s 346`

@export Can the Court of Chancery enjoin or set aside a transfer of the close corporation's stock (s 348(b))?
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the suit brought by the corporation or by a stockholder?
      `the transfer is contrary to the certificate of incorporation or to a restriction permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer, or threatened transfer, contrary to the terms of the certificate of incorporation or to a transfer restriction permitted by s 202?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery enjoin or set aside a transfer of the close corporation's stock` IF
    `s 348(b) the Court of Chancery may enjoin or set aside the transfer or threatened transfer of stock` `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` `the transfer is contrary to the certificate of incorporation or to a restriction permitted by s 202`

@export Can the Court of Chancery enjoin a public offering, or threatened public offering, of the close corporation's stock (s 348(b))?
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the suit brought by the corporation or by a stockholder?
      `there is a public offering or a threatened public offering of the stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public offering, or a threatened public offering, of the corporation's stock (as s 342 defines it)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery enjoin a public offering, or threatened public offering, of the close corporation's stock` IF
    `s 348(b) the Court of Chancery may enjoin the public offering or threatened public offering of stock` `the suit is by the corporation or by a stockholder` `there is a public offering or a threatened public offering of the stock`

-- s 349. The corporation's 30-day option to acquire a security whose transfer restriction was held invalid.
@export By what date may my close corporation exercise its option to acquire a security whose transfer restriction was struck down (s 349)?
GIVEN `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the judgment setting aside the restriction become final?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date may my close corporation exercise its option to acquire a security whose transfer restriction was struck down` IS
    `s 349 the last day of the corporation's option to acquire the restricted security` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final`

@export Can my close corporation still exercise its option to acquire the security on this date (s 349)?
GIVEN `a restriction on transfer was held not authorized by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restriction on transfer of a security of the close corporation held not to be authorized by s 202?
      `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the judgment setting aside the restriction become final?
      `the date the option would be exercised` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the corporation exercise the option?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my close corporation still exercise its option to acquire the security on this date` IF
    `s 349 the corporation may still exercise its option to acquire the restricted security` `a restriction on transfer was held not authorized by s 202` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` `the date the option would be exercised`

@export At what price may my close corporation acquire the security whose restriction was struck down (s 349)?
GIVEN `the parties agreed a price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties agreed on a price?
      `the price they agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what price did they agree, in dollars?
      `the Court of Chancery has determined the fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery determined the fair value?
      `the fair value the Court determined` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fair value did the Court determine, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `At what price may my close corporation acquire the security whose restriction was struck down` IS
    `s 349 the price at which the corporation may acquire the restricted security` (IF `the parties agreed a price` THEN JUST `the price they agreed` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the Court of Chancery has determined the fair value` THEN JUST `the fair value the Court determined` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 350. A written agreement among the stockholders holding a majority of the stock entitled to vote.
@export Is our written agreement as stockholders, which restricts the discretion of the board, invalid as between us on that ground (s 350)?
GIVEN `our agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation (whether solely among themselves or with a party who is not a stockholder)?
      `the votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement?
      `the votes of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote carry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our written agreement as stockholders, which restricts the discretion of the board, invalid as between us on that ground` IS
    `s 350 the agreement is invalid, as between the parties, on the ground that it restricts or interferes with the discretion or powers of the board` (`s 350 the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `our agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` `the votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` `the votes of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)

@export If our stockholders' agreement controls the board, are the directors relieved and are we, as parties, liable for managerial acts or omissions instead (s 350)?
GIVEN `our agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation (whether solely among themselves or with a party who is not a stockholder)?
      `the votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement?
      `the votes of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote carry?
      `the agreement controls the discretion or powers of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement control the discretion or powers of the board in its management of the corporation's affairs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If our stockholders' agreement controls the board, are the directors relieved and are we, as parties, liable for managerial acts or omissions instead` IS
    `s 350 the stockholders who are parties bear the liability for managerial acts or omissions that is imposed on directors, and the directors are relieved` (`s 350 the agreement is a written agreement of stockholders holding a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `our agreement is a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation` `the votes held by the stockholders who are parties to the agreement` `the votes of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the agreement controls the discretion or powers of the board`

-- s 351. Management by the stockholders.
@export Must a meeting of stockholders be called to elect directors when our stockholders manage the corporation (s 351(1))?
GIVEN `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide that the business of the corporation is managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a meeting of stockholders be called to elect directors when our stockholders manage the corporation` IS
    `s 351(1) a meeting of stockholders must be called to elect directors` (`s 351 the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business`)

@export Am I, as a stockholder, treated as a director for the purposes of the Law (s 351(2))?
GIVEN `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide that the business of the corporation is managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors?
      `the context clearly requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision of the Law you are asking about clearly require that stockholders not be treated as directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a stockholder, treated as a director for the purposes of the Law` IS
    `s 351(2) the stockholders are deemed to be directors for purposes of applying the provision of this chapter` (`s 351 the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business`) `the context clearly requires otherwise`

@export Am I, as a stockholder, subject to all the liabilities of a director (s 351(3))?
GIVEN `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide that the business of the corporation is managed by the stockholders rather than by a board of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a stockholder, subject to all the liabilities of a director` IS
    `s 351(3) the stockholders are subject to all liabilities of directors` (`s 351 the provision for management by the stockholders is in effect` `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business`)

@export Can management by the stockholders be added to our certificate of incorporation by amendment (s 351)?
GIVEN `all incorporators and subscribers authorize it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the incorporators and subscribers authorize the provision?
      `all holders of record of all the outstanding stock authorize it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the holders of record of all the outstanding stock, whether or not they have voting power, authorize the provision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can management by the stockholders be added to our certificate of incorporation by amendment` IF
    `s 351 the provision may be inserted in the certificate of incorporation by amendment` `all incorporators and subscribers authorize it` `all holders of record of all the outstanding stock authorize it`

@export Has the amendment deleting management by the stockholders been adopted (s 351)?
GIVEN `the votes held by the holders who voted for the deletion` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are held by the holders who voted for the amendment?
      `the votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock carry, whether or not it is otherwise entitled to vote?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the amendment deleting management by the stockholders been adopted` IS
    `s 351 the amendment deleting the provision is adopted` `the votes held by the holders who voted for the deletion` `the votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote`

@export Does our stock certificate have to note management by the stockholders, and does it (s 351)?
GIVEN `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain the provision for management by the stockholders?
      `the stock certificate notes it conspicuously on its face or back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock certificate note the existence of the provision conspicuously on its face or back?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our stock certificate have to note management by the stockholders, and does it` IF
    `s 351 the stock certificate meets the requirement to note the provision` `our certificate provides that the stockholders manage the business` `the stock certificate notes it conspicuously on its face or back`

-- s 352. Custodian (and receiver, if the corporation is insolvent) on a stockholder's application.
@export Can I, as a stockholder, have the Court of Chancery appoint a custodian or receiver for my close corporation (s 352(a))?
GIVEN `I am applying as a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying as a stockholder?
      `the stockholders manage the corporation under s 351` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the business and affairs of the corporation managed by the stockholders under s 351?
      `the stockholders are so divided that the business is suffering or threatened with irreparable injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the stockholders so divided that the business is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury?
      `every remedy for the deadlock in our certificate, bylaws or a stockholders' agreement has failed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any remedy for the deadlock provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a written agreement of the stockholders failed?
      `I have a right to dissolution under an s 355 provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to dissolution of the corporation under a provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by s 355?
      `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation insolvent?
GIVETH A `s 352(a) Appointment the Court of Chancery may make for a close corporation`
DECIDE `Can I, as a stockholder, have the Court of Chancery appoint a custodian or receiver for my close corporation` IS
    `s 352(a) the appointment the Court of Chancery may make on the application` `I am applying as a stockholder` (`s 352(a)(1) the business is deadlocked and the remedies provided have failed` `the stockholders manage the corporation under s 351` `the stockholders are so divided that the business is suffering or threatened with irreparable injury` `every remedy for the deadlock in our certificate, bylaws or a stockholders' agreement has failed`) (`s 352(a)(2) the petitioning stockholder has a right to dissolution under a provision permitted by s 355` `I have a right to dissolution under an s 355 provision`) `the corporation is insolvent`

@export Can the Court of Chancery appoint a provisional director for my close corporation instead of a custodian (s 352(b))?
GIVEN `a custodian could be appointed under s 352 or s 226` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a custodian be appointed for the corporation under s 352 or s 226?
      `the Court determines that a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court of Chancery determine that appointing a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation? (That is the Court's judgment; say yes only if it has so determined.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a provisional director for my close corporation instead of a custodian` IF
    `s 352(b) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director in lieu of a custodian` `a custodian could be appointed under s 352 or s 226` `the Court determines that a provisional director would be in the best interest of the corporation`

@export If a provisional director is appointed, does that stop the Court from later appointing a custodian (s 352(b))?
GIVEN `a provisional director has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a provisional director been appointed for the corporation under s 352(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If a provisional director is appointed, does that stop the Court from later appointing a custodian` IS
    `s 352(b) the appointment of the provisional director precludes a subsequent order appointing a custodian` `a provisional director has been appointed`

-- s 353. Provisional director.
@export Is my close corporation in a position for the Court of Chancery to appoint a provisional director (s 353(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation?
      `the directors are so divided that the votes needed for board action cannot be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors so divided about the management of the corporation's business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board cannot be obtained?
      `the business can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a consequence, can the business and affairs of the corporation no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my close corporation in a position for the Court of Chancery to appoint a provisional director` IF
    `s 353(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director` `my corporation is a close corporation` `the directors are so divided that the votes needed for board action cannot be obtained` `the business can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally`

@export May our group apply to the Court of Chancery for a provisional director (s 353(b))?
GIVEN `the directors who join in the application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors join in the application?
      `the directors in office` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are then in office?
      `the shares held by the stockholders who join in the application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are held by the stockholders who join in the application?
      `all the shares entitled to elect directors` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are then entitled to elect directors?
      `more than 1 class is entitled to elect directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than 1 class of stock then entitled to elect 1 or more directors?
      `the applicants' shares in the class where they hold the largest proportion` IS A NUMBER @desc Take the class entitled to elect directors in which the applicants hold the largest proportion. How many of its shares do the applicants hold?
      `all the shares of that class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class are there?
      `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation allow a lesser proportion of the directors to apply?
      `that lesser percentage of the directors` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of the directors in office? (Enter 25 for 25%.)
      `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate allow a lesser proportion of the stockholders to apply?
      `that lesser percentage of the stockholders` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of the stock entitled to elect directors? (Enter 25 for 25%.)
      `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate allow a lesser proportion of a class of stockholders to apply?
      `that lesser percentage of a class` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of the class? (Enter 25 for 25%.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our group apply to the Court of Chancery for a provisional director` IS
    `s 353(b) the application may be filed` `our application`
    WHERE
        `our application` MEANS `s 353(b) Application for a provisional director` WITH
            `the number of directors who join in the application` IS `the directors who join in the application`
            `the number of directors then in office` IS `the directors in office`
            `the number of shares held by the stockholders who join in the application` IS `the shares held by the stockholders who join in the application`
            `the number of shares then entitled to elect directors` IS `all the shares entitled to elect directors`
            `more than 1 class of stock is then entitled to elect directors` IS `more than 1 class is entitled to elect directors`
            `the number of shares of the class in which the applicants hold the largest proportion that they hold` IS `the applicants' shares in the class where they hold the largest proportion`
            `the number of shares of that class` IS `all the shares of that class`
            `the lesser proportion of the directors that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one` IS (IF `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of the directors` THEN JUST (`that lesser percentage of the directors` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING)
            `the lesser proportion of the stockholders that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one` IS (IF `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of the stockholders` THEN JUST (`that lesser percentage of the stockholders` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING)
            `the lesser proportion of a class that the certificate of incorporation allows, if it allows one` IS (IF `our certificate allows a lesser proportion of a class` THEN JUST (`that lesser percentage of a class` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING)

@export Can the Court of Chancery appoint a provisional director on our application, counting its power under s 352(b) (s 353)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation?
      `the directors are so divided that the votes needed for board action cannot be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors so divided about the management of the corporation's business and affairs that the votes required for action by the board cannot be obtained?
      `the business can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a consequence, can the business and affairs of the corporation no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally?
      `the application meets s 353(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application meet s 353(b): at least half of the directors in office, or holders of at least one third of the stock entitled to elect directors, or two thirds of a class so entitled (or the lesser proportion the certificate allows)?
      `s 352(b) lets the Court act anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 352(b) permit the Court to appoint a provisional director in place of a custodian in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a provisional director on our application, counting its power under s 352(b)` IS
    `s 353 the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director on the application` (`s 353(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a provisional director` `my corporation is a close corporation` `the directors are so divided that the votes needed for board action cannot be obtained` `the business can no longer be conducted to the advantage of the stockholders generally`) (JUST `the application meets s 353(b)`) `s 352(b) lets the Court act anyway`

@export Can I be appointed a provisional director of this close corporation (s 353(c))?
GIVEN `I am impartial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an impartial person?
      `I am a stockholder of the corporation or of a subsidiary or affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation?
      `I am a creditor of the corporation or of a subsidiary or affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the corporation or of any subsidiary or affiliate of the corporation?
      `I meet the further qualifications the Court sets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet any further qualifications that the Court of Chancery determines?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be appointed a provisional director of this close corporation` IF
    `s 353(c) the person may be appointed a provisional director` `I am impartial` `I am a stockholder of the corporation or of a subsidiary or affiliate` `I am a creditor of the corporation or of a subsidiary or affiliate` `I meet the further qualifications the Court sets`

@export As a provisional director, do I have the rights and powers of a duly elected director, including notice of and a vote at board meetings (s 353(c))?
GIVEN `I am a provisional director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a provisional director appointed under s 353?
      `I have been removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been removed by order of the Court of Chancery or by a vote of the stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a provisional director, do I have the rights and powers of a duly elected director, including notice of and a vote at board meetings` IS
    `s 353(c) the provisional director has all the rights and powers of a duly elected director, including notice of and a vote at meetings of directors` `I am a provisional director` `I have been removed`

@export As a provisional director, am I a receiver with the title and powers of a custodian or receiver (s 353(c))?
GIVEN `I am a provisional director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a provisional director appointed under s 353?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a provisional director, am I a receiver with the title and powers of a custodian or receiver` IS
    `s 353(c) the provisional director has the title and powers of a custodian or receiver` `I am a provisional director`

@export Can the provisional director be removed (s 353(c))?
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered removal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery ordered the provisional director removed?
      `the votes for removal among all shares entitled to vote to elect directors` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast to remove the provisional director by the holders of shares entitled to vote to elect directors?
      `the votes of all shares entitled to vote to elect directors` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do all the shares then entitled to vote to elect directors carry?
      `a class of voting shares filed the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application for the provisional director filed by the holders of a class of voting shares?
      `the votes for removal among that class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast to remove the provisional director by the holders of that class?
      `the votes of that class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does that class carry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the provisional director be removed` IS
    `s 353(c) the provisional director is removed` `the Court of Chancery has ordered removal` `the votes for removal among all shares entitled to vote to elect directors` `the votes of all shares entitled to vote to elect directors` `a class of voting shares filed the application` `the votes for removal among that class` `the votes of that class`

@export How is my compensation as provisional director determined (s 353(c))?
GIVEN `the provisional director and the corporation agreed my compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the provisional director and the corporation agreed the compensation?
      `the Court of Chancery has approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery approved the agreement?
GIVETH A `s 353(c) How the provisional director's compensation is determined`
DECIDE `How is my compensation as provisional director determined` IS
    `s 353(c) the provisional director's compensation is determined` `the provisional director and the corporation agreed my compensation` `the Court of Chancery has approved the agreement`

-- s 354. An agreement or provision is not invalid for treating the corporation as a partnership.
@export Is our stockholders' agreement, or this provision of the certificate or bylaws, invalid because it treats the corporation as a partnership (s 354)?
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 354 Instrument of a close corporation` @desc What is it: a written agreement among stockholders of a close corporation, a provision of its certificate of incorporation, a provision of its bylaws, or something else?
      `it relates to a phase of the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to any phase of the affairs of the corporation (management, dividends or profit division, election of directors or officers, employment of stockholders, arbitration of disputes, or the like)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our stockholders' agreement, or this provision of the certificate or bylaws, invalid because it treats the corporation as a partnership` IS
    `s 354 the instrument is invalid on the ground that it treats the corporation as a partnership` instrument `it relates to a phase of the affairs of the corporation`

-- s 355. The stockholders' option to dissolve the corporation.
@export May I exercise the option in our certificate of incorporation to have the corporation dissolved (s 355(a))?
GIVEN `our certificate includes a provision granting an option to have the corporation dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation include a provision granting a stockholder, or holders of a specified number or percentage of shares of a class, an option to have the corporation dissolved?
      `I am a stockholder who holds, alone or with others, what the provision specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder, or do you hold with others the number or percentage of shares of a class that the provision specifies?
      `the option is at will or the specified event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the option exercisable at will, or has the specified event or contingency occurred?
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I exercise the option in our certificate of incorporation to have the corporation dissolved` IF
    `s 355(a) the option to have the corporation dissolved may be exercised` `our certificate includes a provision granting an option to have the corporation dissolved` `I am a stockholder who holds, alone or with others, what the provision specifies` `the option is at will or the specified event has occurred` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate`

@export When does the dissolution proceed after we give notice that we exercise the option to dissolve (s 355(a))?
GIVEN `the date we sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice sent to all the other stockholders?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does the dissolution proceed after we give notice that we exercise the option to dissolve` IS
    `s 355(a) the first day on which the dissolution proceeds` `the date we sent the notice`

@export Does the dissolution now proceed as if the required stockholders had consented in writing under s 228 (s 355(a))?
GIVEN `we exercised the option in accordance with s 355(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the option exercised by a person entitled to exercise it?
      `our notice was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of the exercise in writing?
      `our notice was given to all the other stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given to all the other stockholders?
      `the date we sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice sent?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date do you want to know whether the dissolution proceeds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the dissolution now proceed as if the required stockholders had consented in writing under s 228` IF
    `s 355(a) the dissolution proceeds as if the required stockholders had consented in writing under s 228` `we exercised the option in accordance with s 355(a)` (`s 355(a) the notice of the exercise of the option meets the subsection` `our notice was in writing` `our notice was given to all the other stockholders`) `the date we sent the notice` `the date I am asking about`

@export Has the amendment adding an option to dissolve been adopted (s 355(b))?
GIVEN `the original certificate did not contain an option to dissolve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation as originally filed lack a provision granting an option to dissolve?
      `our certificate authorizes such an amendment by a lesser vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate specifically authorize such an amendment by a vote of less than all the outstanding stock?
      `the percentage of all the outstanding stock it requires` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote, does it require? (Enter 75 for 75%. The Law allows no less than two thirds.)
      `the votes cast for the amendment by all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for the amendment, counting all the outstanding stock whether or not it is entitled to vote?
      `the votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock carry, whether or not it is entitled to vote?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the amendment adding an option to dissolve been adopted` IS
    `s 355(b) the amendment adding the option to dissolve is adopted` `the original certificate did not contain an option to dissolve` (IF `our certificate authorizes such an amendment by a lesser vote` THEN JUST (`the percentage of all the outstanding stock it requires` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING) `the votes cast for the amendment by all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote` `the votes of all the outstanding stock, whether or not entitled to vote`

@export Does my stock certificate have to note the option to dissolve, and does it (s 355(c))?
GIVEN `our certificate authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation authorize dissolution as s 355 permits?
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my stock certificate have to note the option to dissolve, and does it` IF
    `s 355(c) the stock certificate meets the requirement to note the provision` `our certificate authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate`

@export Is the option to dissolve effective as to my stock certificate (s 355(c))?
GIVEN `our certificate authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation authorize dissolution as s 355 permits?
      `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision noted conspicuously on the face of the stock certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the option to dissolve effective as to my stock certificate` IS
    `s 355(c) the provision is effective as to the holder of the stock certificate` `our certificate authorizes dissolution as permitted by s 355` `the provision is noted conspicuously on the face of my stock certificate`

-- s 356. Effect of the subchapter on other laws.
@export Does the close corporation subchapter repeal a law that applies to my corporation, which is not a close corporation (s 356)?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the General Corporation Law?
      `my corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a close corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the close corporation subchapter repeal a law that applies to my corporation, which is not a close corporation` IS
    `s 356 this subchapter repeals a statute or rule of law applicable to the corporation` `my corporation is organized under the General Corporation Law` `my corporation is a close corporation`

§§ `My public benefit corporation (s 361 to s 368)`

-- Situation: only if your corporation is, or is becoming, a public benefit corporation.

-- s 361. Which requirement applies.
@export Does the public benefit corporation subchapter apply to my corporation (s 361)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a public benefit corporation as s 362 defines it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the public benefit corporation subchapter apply to my corporation` IF
    `s 361 this subchapter applies to the corporation` `my corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362`

@export On this point, does the public benefit corporation subchapter's requirement apply in place of the General Corporation Law's (s 361)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a public benefit corporation as s 362 defines it?
      `the subchapter imposes an additional or different requirement on this point` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subchapter XV (ss 361 to 368) impose an additional or different requirement on the point you are asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `On this point, does the public benefit corporation subchapter's requirement apply in place of the General Corporation Law's` IS
    `s 361 the requirement of this subchapter applies in place of the requirement of this chapter` `my corporation is a public benefit corporation as defined in s 362` `the subchapter imposes an additional or different requirement on this point`

-- s 362(a). A public benefit corporation: for-profit, organized under the chapter, intended to produce a public benefit
-- and to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner.
@export Is my corporation a public benefit corporation (s 362(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of the General Corporation Law?
      `my corporation is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits?
      `my corporation is intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation a public benefit corporation` IF
    `s 362(a) the corporation is a public benefit corporation` `our corporation`
    WHERE
        `our corporation` MEANS `s 362(a) Corporation said to be a public benefit corporation` WITH
            `the corporation is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the requirements of this chapter` IS `my corporation is a for-profit corporation organized under and subject to the General Corporation Law`
            `the corporation is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits` IS `my corporation is intended to produce a public benefit or public benefits`
            `the corporation is intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner` IS `my corporation is intended to operate in a responsible and sustainable manner`

@export Does our certificate of incorporation say what a public benefit corporation's certificate must say (s 362(a)(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the number of specific public benefits our statement of business or purpose identifies` IS A NUMBER @desc How many specific public benefits does the statement of business or purpose in the certificate of incorporation identify?
      `our certificate states in its heading that we are a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation state within its heading that the corporation is a public benefit corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our certificate of incorporation say what a public benefit corporation's certificate must say` IF
        `s 362(a)(1) the certificate identifies within its statement of business or purpose one or more specific public benefits` `the number of specific public benefits our statement of business or purpose identifies`
    AND `s 362(a)(2) the certificate states within its heading that it is a public benefit corporation` `our certificate states in its heading that we are a public benefit corporation`

@export Does the board manage in the way a public benefit corporation must be managed, balancing the three interests (s 362(a), s 365(a))?
GIVEN `we balance the stockholders' pecuniary interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the board balance the stockholders' pecuniary interests?
      `we balance the best interests of those materially affected by our conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the board balance the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation's conduct?
      `we balance the public benefit or benefits identified in our certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the board balance the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the board manage in the way a public benefit corporation must be managed, balancing the three interests` IF
    `s 365(a) the board manages or directs the business and affairs in a manner that balances the three interests` `our balance`
    WHERE
        `our balance` MEANS `s 362(a) Balancing of interests` WITH
            `the stockholders' pecuniary interests are balanced` IS `we balance the stockholders' pecuniary interests`
            `the best interests of those materially affected by the corporation's conduct are balanced` IS `we balance the best interests of those materially affected by our conduct`
            `the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation are balanced` IS `we balance the public benefit or benefits identified in our certificate`

-- s 362(b). What a public benefit is.
@export Is this effect a "public benefit" for the purposes of the Law (s 362(b))?
GIVEN `the effect is a positive effect or a reduction of negative effects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the effect a positive effect, or a reduction of negative effects?
      `it is on categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders as stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on 1 or more categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders in their capacities as stockholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this effect a "public benefit" for the purposes of the Law` IF
    `s 362(b) the effect is a public benefit` `the effect is a positive effect or a reduction of negative effects` `it is on categories of persons, entities, communities or interests other than stockholders as stockholders`

-- s 362(c). The name, and the notice owed on issuing stock when the name does not say.
@export Does our corporation's name satisfy the name requirement of section 102(a)(1)(i) by carrying a public benefit corporation designation (s 362(c))?
GIVEN `our name contains the words "public benefit corporation"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain the words "public benefit corporation"?
      `our name contains the abbreviation "P.B.C."` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain the abbreviation "P.B.C."?
      `our name contains the designation "PBC"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain the designation "PBC"?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our corporation's name satisfy the name requirement of section 102(a)(1)(i) by carrying a public benefit corporation designation` IF
    `s 362(c) the name is deemed to satisfy the requirements of s 102(a)(1)(i)` `our name contains the words "public benefit corporation"` `our name contains the abbreviation "P.B.C."` `our name contains the designation "PBC"`

@export Must our public benefit corporation give notice that it is one before issuing or disposing of stock (s 362(c))?
GIVEN `we are issuing unissued shares or disposing of treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation issuing unissued shares of stock or disposing of treasury shares?
      `our name contains one of the public benefit corporation designations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's name contain the words "public benefit corporation", or "P.B.C.", or "PBC"?
      `the issuance or disposal is under an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuance or disposal pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933?
      `we have a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the issuance or disposal, does the corporation have a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our public benefit corporation give notice that it is one before issuing or disposing of stock` IF
    `s 362(c) the corporation must give notice that it is a public benefit corporation to the person who acquires the stock` `we are issuing unissued shares or disposing of treasury shares` `our name contains one of the public benefit corporation designations` `the issuance or disposal is under an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` `we have a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934`

@export Am I entitled to be told that the corporation is a public benefit corporation when I acquire its stock (s 362(c))?
GIVEN `I am acquiring unissued shares or treasury shares from the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you acquiring unissued shares of stock, or treasury shares, from the corporation?
      `its name contains one of the public benefit corporation designations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's name contain the words "public benefit corporation", or "P.B.C.", or "PBC"?
      `my acquisition is under an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your acquisition pursuant to an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933?
      `it has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of your acquisition, does the corporation have a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be told that the corporation is a public benefit corporation when I acquire its stock` IF
    `s 362(c) the corporation must give notice that it is a public benefit corporation to the person who acquires the stock` `I am acquiring unissued shares or treasury shares from the corporation` `its name contains one of the public benefit corporation designations` `my acquisition is under an offering registered under the Securities Act of 1933` `it has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934`

-- s 363. A nonprofit nonstock corporation may not merge with a public benefit corporation.
@export Can my nonprofit nonstock corporation be a constituent corporation to a merger or consolidation with a public benefit corporation (s 363)?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the merger or consolidation is with a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the merger or consolidation with a public benefit corporation?
      `the surviving corporation's certificate is amended to add a s 362(a)(1) provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation amended to include a provision authorized by s 362(a)(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my nonprofit nonstock corporation be a constituent corporation to a merger or consolidation with a public benefit corporation` IS
    `s 363 the corporation may be a constituent corporation to the merger or consolidation` `the kind of my corporation` `the merger or consolidation is with a public benefit corporation` `the surviving corporation's certificate is amended to add a s 362(a)(1) provision`

-- s 364. What the stock certificate and the s 151(f) notice must say.
@export Does our stock certificate note, as the Law requires, that we are a public benefit corporation (s 364)?
GIVEN `our stock certificate notes conspicuously that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock certificate note conspicuously that the corporation is a public benefit corporation formed pursuant to Subchapter XV?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our stock certificate note, as the Law requires, that we are a public benefit corporation` IF
    `s 364 the stock certificate meets the requirement to note that the corporation is a public benefit corporation` `our stock certificate notes conspicuously that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter`

@export Does our notice about uncertificated stock state, as the Law requires, that we are a public benefit corporation (s 364)?
GIVEN `our notice under s 151(f) states conspicuously that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice given under s 151(f) state conspicuously that the corporation is a public benefit corporation formed pursuant to Subchapter XV?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our notice about uncertificated stock state, as the Law requires, that we are a public benefit corporation` IF
    `s 364 the notice meets the requirement to state that the corporation is a public benefit corporation` `our notice under s 151(f) states conspicuously that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter`

-- s 365. Duties of directors of a public benefit corporation.
@export As a director of a public benefit corporation, do I owe a duty to the people the public benefit reaches, by virtue of the public benefit provisions (s 365(b))?
GIVEN `the duty would be on account of that person's interest in the public benefit identified in our certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the duty be on account of the person's interest in the public benefit or public benefits identified in the certificate of incorporation?
      `the duty would be on account of an interest materially affected by our conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the duty be on account of an interest materially affected by the corporation's conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director of a public benefit corporation, do I owe a duty to the people the public benefit reaches, by virtue of the public benefit provisions` IS
    `s 365(b) the director has a duty to the person by virtue of the public benefit provisions or s 362(a)` `the duty would be on account of that person's interest in the public benefit identified in our certificate` `the duty would be on account of an interest materially affected by our conduct`

@export As a director of a public benefit corporation, am I deemed to have satisfied my fiduciary duties on this decision (s 365(b))?
GIVEN `the decision implicates the balance requirement in s 365(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision implicate the balance requirement in s 365(a)?
      `my decision is informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your decision informed?
      `my decision is disinterested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your decision disinterested?
      `no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve my decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your decision such that no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve it? (That is a judgment you state.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director of a public benefit corporation, am I deemed to have satisfied my fiduciary duties on this decision` IS
    `s 365(b) the director is deemed to satisfy the director's fiduciary duties to the stockholders and the corporation` `the decision implicates the balance requirement in s 365(a)` `my decision is informed` `my decision is disinterested` `no person of ordinary, sound judgment would approve my decision`

@export Does my stock ownership create a conflict of interest on the balancing decision of a public benefit corporation (s 365(c))?
GIVEN `my stock interest would create a conflict if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your ownership of or interest in the corporation's stock create a conflict of interest if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my stock ownership create a conflict of interest on the balancing decision of a public benefit corporation` IF
    `s 365(c) the director's ownership of or interest in the stock creates a conflict of interest for the balancing decision` `my stock interest would create a conflict if the corporation were not a public benefit corporation`

@export Is a failure to satisfy the balancing requirement a lack of good faith or a breach of loyalty for sections 102(b)(7) and 145 (s 365(c))?
GIVEN `there is a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a conflict of interest?
      `our certificate of incorporation so provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide that such a failure is an act or omission not in good faith or a breach of the duty of loyalty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a failure to satisfy the balancing requirement a lack of good faith or a breach of loyalty for sections 102(b)(7) and 145` IS
    `s 365(c) a failure to satisfy the balancing requirement is an act or omission not in good faith, or a breach of the duty of loyalty, for the purposes of s 102(b)(7) or s 145` `there is a conflict of interest` `our certificate of incorporation so provides`

-- s 366. Statements to the stockholders.
@export Does the notice of the stockholders' meeting include the statement that we are a public benefit corporation (s 366(a))?
GIVEN `our notice of the meeting includes the statement that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice of the meeting of stockholders include a statement to the effect that the corporation is a public benefit corporation formed pursuant to Subchapter XV?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the stockholders' meeting include the statement that we are a public benefit corporation` IF
    `s 366(a) the notice of the meeting meets the requirement to include the statement` `our notice of the meeting includes the statement that we are a public benefit corporation formed under this subchapter`

@export How many months may pass between our statements to the stockholders on the public benefit (s 366(b), (c)(1))?
GIVEN `where a provision requiring more frequent statements is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the provision requiring statements more often than every two years: the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a board resolution, or nowhere?
      `the number of months between statements that it requires` IS A NUMBER @desc If there is such a provision, how many months does it allow between statements?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months may pass between our statements to the stockholders on the public benefit` IS
    `s 366(c)(1) the number of months between statements` `where a provision requiring more frequent statements is made` `the number of months between statements that it requires`

@export By what date must we give the stockholders the next statement on the public benefit (s 366(b))?
GIVEN `we have given a statement before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation given its stockholders a statement on the public benefit before?
      `the date we last gave the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last statement provided?
      `the number of months between statements` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months may pass between statements? (24 unless the certificate or bylaws require them more often.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what date must we give the stockholders the next statement on the public benefit` IS
    `s 366(b) the last day for the next statement` (IF `we have given a statement before` THEN JUST `the date we last gave the statement` ELSE NOTHING) `the number of months between statements`

@export Did we give the stockholders the next statement on the public benefit in time (s 366(b))?
GIVEN `we have given a statement before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation given its stockholders a statement on the public benefit before?
      `the date we last gave the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last statement provided?
      `the number of months between statements` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months may pass between statements? (24 unless the certificate or bylaws require them more often.)
      `the date we gave the next statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the next statement provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did we give the stockholders the next statement on the public benefit in time` IS
    `s 366(b) the next statement was provided in time` (IF `we have given a statement before` THEN JUST `the date we last gave the statement` ELSE NOTHING) `the number of months between statements` `the date we gave the next statement`

@export Does our statement to the stockholders include everything the Law requires (s 366(b))?
GIVEN `it gives the objectives the board has established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the objectives the board of directors has established to promote the public benefit or benefits and interests?
      `it gives the standards the board has adopted to measure progress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the standards the board has adopted to measure the corporation's progress?
      `it gives objective factual information based on those standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give objective factual information, based on those standards, about the corporation's success in meeting the objectives?
      `it gives an assessment of our success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give an assessment of the corporation's success in meeting the objectives and promoting the public benefit or benefits and interests?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our statement to the stockholders include everything the Law requires` IF
    `s 366(b) the statement includes what the subsection requires` `our statement`
    WHERE
        `our statement` MEANS `s 366(b) Statement to the stockholders` WITH
            `the statement gives the objectives the board of directors has established to promote the public benefit or public benefits and interests` IS `it gives the objectives the board has established`
            `the statement gives the standards the board of directors has adopted to measure the corporation's progress` IS `it gives the standards the board has adopted to measure progress`
            `the statement gives objective factual information based on those standards regarding the corporation's success in meeting the objectives` IS `it gives objective factual information based on those standards`
            `the statement gives an assessment of the corporation's success in meeting the objectives and promoting the public benefit or public benefits and interests` IS `it gives an assessment of our success`

@export Must our public benefit corporation make its statement available to the public (s 366(c)(2))?
GIVEN `where the provision requiring public availability is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the provision requiring the statement to be made available to the public: the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a board resolution, or nowhere?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our public benefit corporation make its statement available to the public` IF
    `s 366(c)(2) the corporation must make the statement available to the public` `where the provision requiring public availability is made`

@export Must our public benefit corporation use a third-party standard or attain a periodic third-party certification (s 366(c)(3))?
GIVEN `where the provision requiring a third-party standard is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the provision requiring a third-party standard or certification: the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a board resolution, or nowhere?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our public benefit corporation use a third-party standard or attain a periodic third-party certification` IF
    `s 366(c)(3) the corporation must use a third-party standard or attain a periodic third-party certification` `where the provision requiring a third-party standard is made`

-- s 367. Who may sue to enforce the balancing requirement.
@export Do my fellow plaintiffs and I own enough shares to sue to enforce the balancing requirement (s 367)?
GIVEN `the shares we own individually or together on the day we sue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do the plaintiffs own, individually or collectively, as of the date of instituting the action?
      `the corporation's outstanding shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the corporation are outstanding?
      `the corporation's shares are listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have shares listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the market value of our shares in dollars on the day we sue` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the market value, in dollars, of the plaintiffs' shares as of the date the action is instituted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my fellow plaintiffs and I own enough shares to sue to enforce the balancing requirement` IS
    `s 367 the plaintiffs own enough shares to bring the action` `the shares we own individually or together on the day we sue` `the corporation's outstanding shares` `the corporation's shares are listed on a national securities exchange` `the market value of our shares in dollars on the day we sue`

@export May my fellow plaintiffs and I bring the action to enforce the balancing requirement (s 367)?
GIVEN `the shares we own individually or together on the day we sue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do the plaintiffs own, individually or collectively, as of the date of instituting the action?
      `the corporation's outstanding shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the corporation are outstanding?
      `the corporation's shares are listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have shares listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the market value of our shares in dollars on the day we sue` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the market value, in dollars, of the plaintiffs' shares as of the date the action is instituted?
      `our action is a derivative action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a derivative action?
      `our complaint makes the s 327 averment of stock ownership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the complaint contain the averment of stock ownership that s 327 requires?
      `we comply with the court's rules and any other conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the plaintiffs comply with any other conditions applicable to filing a derivative action, including the rules of the court in which the action is filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fellow plaintiffs and I bring the action to enforce the balancing requirement` IS
    `s 367 the plaintiffs may bring the action to enforce the balancing requirement` (`s 367 the plaintiffs own enough shares to bring the action` `the shares we own individually or together on the day we sue` `the corporation's outstanding shares` `the corporation's shares are listed on a national securities exchange` `the market value of our shares in dollars on the day we sue`) `our action is a derivative action` `our complaint makes the s 327 averment of stock ownership` `we comply with the court's rules and any other conditions`

-- s 368. No effect on other corporations.
@export Does the public benefit corporation subchapter affect a law that applies to my corporation, which is not a public benefit corporation (s 368)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a public benefit corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a public benefit corporation?
      `the law is one that s 363 provides for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the law one that s 363 provides for (a nonprofit nonstock corporation's merger with a public benefit corporation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the public benefit corporation subchapter affect a law that applies to my corporation, which is not a public benefit corporation` IS
    `s 368 this subchapter affects the statute or rule of law applicable to the corporation` `my corporation is a public benefit corporation` `the law is one that s 363 provides for`

§§ `A foreign corporation doing business in Delaware (s 371 to s 385)`

-- Situation: only if your corporation is organized outside Delaware and does, or wants to do, business in Delaware,
-- or you deal with, serve or sue such a corporation.

-- s 371(a).
@export Is my corporation a "foreign corporation" under the Delaware General Corporation Law (s 371(a))?
GIVEN `where my corporation is organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is the corporation organized: Delaware, another US jurisdiction, or a jurisdiction outside the United States?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation a "foreign corporation" under the Delaware General Corporation Law` IF
    `s 371(a) the corporation is a foreign corporation` `where my corporation is organized`

-- s 371(b). Qualifying: $80, a certificate of corporate existence not more than 6 months old, and a statement naming
-- an allowed registered agent, with assets and liabilities not more than 6 months old, and the business proposed.
@export Is the registered agent we chose one that the Law allows for a foreign corporation (s 371(b)(2)(i))?
GIVEN `the agent is our own foreign corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registered agent the foreign corporation itself?
      `the kind of the agent` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of person or entity is the registered agent: a natural person, a corporation, a partnership of one of the four kinds, a limited liability company, a statutory trust, or another kind of entity?
      `the agent is an individual resident in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the agent is an individual: does the individual reside in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the registered agent we chose one that the Law allows for a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 371(b)(2)(i) the registered agent is one that the subparagraph allows` `the agent is our own foreign corporation itself` `the kind of the agent` `the agent is an individual resident in Delaware`

@export Has my foreign corporation paid and filed what it needs to do business in Delaware (s 371(b))?
GIVEN `the amount we paid the Secretary of State` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the foreign corporation pay the Secretary of State of Delaware for the use of the State, in dollars?
      `the date we filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the foreign corporation file with the Secretary of State?
      `the date of our certificate of corporate existence` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the certificate evidencing the corporation's corporate existence?
      `the certificate was issued by an authorized officer of our home jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of incorporation?
      `the certificate evidences our corporate existence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate evidence the corporation's corporate existence?
      `the certificate is in a foreign language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate in a foreign language?
      `a translation under oath of the translator is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is a translation of it, under oath of the translator, attached?
      `our statement was executed by an authorized officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement executed by an authorized officer of the corporation?
      `our statement names our registered agent and gives the agent's address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set forth the name and address of the corporation's registered agent in Delaware?
      `the agent is one the Law allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that agent one the Law allows (see the question on the registered agent)?
      `the date as of which our statement of assets and liabilities is made` IS A DATE @desc As of what date is the statement of the corporation's assets and liabilities made?
      `our statement sets forth our assets and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set forth the assets and liabilities of the corporation?
      `our statement sets forth the business we propose to do here and that we are authorized to do it at home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set forth the business the corporation proposes to do in Delaware and say that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation?
      `our statement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement acknowledged in accordance with s 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my foreign corporation paid and filed what it needs to do business in Delaware` IF
    `s 371(b) the foreign corporation has paid and filed what the subsection requires` `the amount we paid the Secretary of State` `our certificate of corporate existence` `our statement` `the date we filed`
    WHERE
        `our certificate of corporate existence` MEANS `s 371(b)(1) Certificate of corporate existence` WITH
            `the date of the certificate` IS `the date of our certificate of corporate existence`
            `the certificate was issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of incorporation` IS `the certificate was issued by an authorized officer of our home jurisdiction`
            `the certificate evidences the foreign corporation's corporate existence` IS `the certificate evidences our corporate existence`
            `the certificate is in a foreign language` IS `the certificate is in a foreign language`
            `a translation of the certificate, under oath of the translator, is attached` IS `a translation under oath of the translator is attached`
        `our statement` MEANS `s 371(b)(2) Statement of the foreign corporation` WITH
            `the statement was executed by an authorized officer of the corporation` IS `our statement was executed by an authorized officer`
            `the statement sets forth the name and address of its registered agent in this State` IS `our statement names our registered agent and gives the agent's address`
            `the registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows` IS `the agent is one the Law allows`
            `the date as of which the statement of the assets and liabilities of the corporation is made` IS `the date as of which our statement of assets and liabilities is made`
            `the statement sets forth the assets and liabilities of the corporation` IS `our statement sets forth our assets and liabilities`
            `the statement sets forth the business the corporation proposes to do in this State and that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation` IS `our statement sets forth the business we propose to do here and that we are authorized to do it at home`
            `the statement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS `our statement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103`

@export May my foreign corporation do business in Delaware through branch offices, agents or representatives located here (s 371(b))?
GIVEN `we have paid and filed what s 371(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the foreign corporation paid the $80 and filed the certificate of corporate existence and the statement that s 371(b) requires?
      `s 373(a) excuses us from ss 371 and 372` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign corporation excused from ss 371 and 372 by one of the exceptions in s 373(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my foreign corporation do business in Delaware through branch offices, agents or representatives located here` IF
    `s 371(b) the foreign corporation may do business in this State through branch offices, agents or representatives located here` `we have paid and filed what s 371(b) requires` `s 373(a) excuses us from ss 371 and 372`

-- s 371(c). The Secretary of State's certificate and the name.
@export Is the Secretary of State's certificate that we filed prima facie evidence of our right to do business in Delaware (s 371(c))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State delivered the certificate of the filing to our registered agent on payment of the fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State deliver the certificate of the filing to the corporation's registered agent upon payment of the fee prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State's certificate that we filed prima facie evidence of our right to do business in Delaware` IF
    `s 371(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the right to do business in this State` `the Secretary of State delivered the certificate of the filing to our registered agent on payment of the fee`

@export May the Secretary of State issue the certificate of filing for my foreign corporation under this name (s 371(c))?
GIVEN `our name distinguishes us on the Division of Corporations' records from reserved names and other entities' names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's name distinguish it upon the records of the Division of Corporations from the names that are reserved and from the names of each other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust organized or registered in Delaware (domestic or foreign)?
      `the person who reserved the name or the other entity consented in a filed writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who reserved the name, or the other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust, consented in writing, executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with s 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State issue the certificate of filing for my foreign corporation under this name` IF
    `s 371(c) the Secretary of State may issue the certificate as to the name` `our name distinguishes us on the Division of Corporations' records from reserved names and other entities' names` `the person who reserved the name or the other entity consented in a filed writing`

@export If our name conflicts with another name, may my foreign corporation qualify to do business under an assumed name (s 371(c))?
GIVEN `our name conflicts with another name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's name conflict with the name of a Delaware (or registered foreign) corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust, or with a reserved name?
      `we adopt an assumed name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation adopt an assumed name to use when doing business in Delaware?
      `the assumed name is authorized for use by s 371(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assumed name authorized for use by s 371(c) (it does not conflict in the same way)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If our name conflicts with another name, may my foreign corporation qualify to do business under an assumed name` IF
    `s 371(c) the foreign corporation may qualify to do business under an assumed name` `our name conflicts with another name` `we adopt an assumed name` `the assumed name is authorized for use by s 371(c)`

-- s 372. Changes after qualifying.
@export By what date must my foreign corporation file a certificate after changing its name or its business in Delaware (s 372(a))?
GIVEN `the date our change becomes effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the change of name, or the enlargement, limitation or other change of business, become effective?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my foreign corporation file a certificate after changing its name or its business in Delaware` IS
    `s 372(a) the last day for the foreign corporation to file the certificate of change` `the date our change becomes effective`

@export Does our certificate of change set forth everything s 372(a) requires (s 372(a))?
GIVEN `we changed our corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the foreign corporation change its corporate name?
      `we enlarged, limited or otherwise changed our business in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the foreign corporation enlarge, limit or otherwise change the business it proposes to do in Delaware?
      `it gives our name as it appears on the Secretary of State's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate give the name as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State?
      `it gives our jurisdiction of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate give the jurisdiction of incorporation?
      `it gives the date we were authorized to do business in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate give the date the corporation was authorized to do business in Delaware?
      `it states the name we relinquished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the name changed: does it state the name relinquished?
      `it states our new name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the name changed: does it state the new name?
      `it states the change of name was effected under our home law, and the date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the name changed: does it state that the change was effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of incorporation, and the date it was effected?
      `it contains a statement reflecting the change in our business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the business changed: does it contain a statement reflecting the change?
      `it states that we are authorized at home to do the business we propose here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the business changed: does it state that the corporation is authorized to do in its home jurisdiction the business it proposes to do in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our certificate of change set forth everything s 372(a) requires` IF
    `s 372(a) the certificate of change sets forth what the subsection requires` `our certificate of change`
    WHERE
        `our certificate of change` MEANS `s 372(a) Certificate of change` WITH
            `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name` IS `we changed our corporate name`
            `the foreign corporation enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State` IS `we enlarged, limited or otherwise changed our business in Delaware`
            `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State` IS `it gives our name as it appears on the Secretary of State's records`
            `the certificate sets forth the jurisdiction of its incorporation` IS `it gives our jurisdiction of incorporation`
            `the certificate sets forth the date it was authorized to do business in this State` IS `it gives the date we were authorized to do business in Delaware`
            `the certificate states the name relinquished` IS `it states the name we relinquished`
            `the certificate states the new name` IS `it states our new name`
            `the certificate states that the change of name has been effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation and the date it was effected` IS `it states the change of name was effected under our home law, and the date`
            `the certificate contains a statement reflecting the change in the business` IS `it contains a statement reflecting the change in our business`
            `the certificate states that the foreign corporation is authorized to do in the jurisdiction of its incorporation the business it proposes to do in this State` IS `it states that we are authorized at home to do the business we propose here`

@export By what date must the surviving foreign corporation file the certificate attesting to a merger (s 372(b))?
GIVEN `the date the merger becomes effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the merger become effective?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the surviving foreign corporation file the certificate attesting to a merger` IS
    `s 372(b) the last day for the surviving foreign corporation to file the certificate attesting to the merger` `the date the merger becomes effective`

@export Is our certificate attesting to the merger what s 372(b) requires (s 372(b))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued by the proper officer of our home state or country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate issued by the proper officer of the state or country of incorporation?
      `the certificate attests to the occurrence of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate attest to the occurrence of the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our certificate attesting to the merger what s 372(b) requires` IF
    `s 372(b) the certificate attesting to the merger is as the subsection requires` `the certificate was issued by the proper officer of our home state or country` `the certificate attests to the occurrence of the merger`

@export Must the surviving foreign corporation also file the certificate of change that s 372(a) describes (s 372(b))?
GIVEN `the merger changed our corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the merger change the corporate name of the foreign corporation?
      `the merger enlarged, limited or otherwise changed our business in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the merger enlarge, limit or otherwise change the business the corporation proposes to do in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the surviving foreign corporation also file the certificate of change that s 372(a) describes` IF
    `s 372(b) the surviving foreign corporation must also comply with subsection (a)` `the merger changed our corporate name` `the merger enlarged, limited or otherwise changed our business in Delaware`

@export Must my foreign corporation withdraw as s 381 provides because it ceased to exist in a merger or consolidation (s 372(c))?
GIVEN `we cease to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the foreign corporation cease to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my foreign corporation withdraw as s 381 provides because it ceased to exist in a merger or consolidation` IF
    `s 372(c) the foreign corporation must comply with s 381` `we cease to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation`

@export What must my foreign corporation pay the Secretary of State for its filings after a change (s 372(d))?
GIVEN `the number of certificates we file under s 372(a) or (b)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many certificates does the foreign corporation file under s 372(a) or (b)?
      `we changed our corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the foreign corporation change its corporate name?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must my foreign corporation pay the Secretary of State for its filings after a change` IS
    `s 372(d) the amount to be paid to the Secretary of State` `the number of certificates we file under s 372(a) or (b)` `we changed our corporate name`

-- s 373. Exceptions: the seven conditions under which a foreign corporation need not comply with ss 371 and 372.
@export Is my foreign corporation excused from the qualification requirements of ss 371 and 372 (s 373(a))?
GIVEN `we are in the mail order or a similar business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign corporation in the mail order or a similar business?
      `we merely receive orders by mail or otherwise from letters, catalogs or other advertising` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it merely receive orders by mail or otherwise in pursuance of letters, circulars, catalogs or other forms of advertising or solicitation?
      `we accept the orders outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it accept the orders outside Delaware?
      `we fill them with goods shipped into Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it fill them with goods shipped into Delaware?
      `we employ salespersons to solicit orders in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it employ salespersons, resident or traveling, to solicit orders in Delaware?
      `all orders are subject to approval at our offices outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all orders subject to approval at its offices outside Delaware?
      `all goods are shipped from outside Delaware to the vendee or the seller's agent for delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all goods applicable to the orders shipped from outside Delaware to the vendee, or to the seller or the seller's agent for delivery to the vendee?
      `we keep samples in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it keep samples in Delaware?
      `our samples in Delaware are for display or advertising only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are they for display or advertising purposes only?
      `no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are no sales, repairs or replacements made from stock on hand in Delaware?
      `we sell by contract consummated outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it sell by contract consummated outside Delaware?
      `we agree to deliver into Delaware machinery, plants or equipment needing installation supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it agree by the contract to deliver into Delaware machinery, plants or equipment whose construction, erection or installation requires the supervision of technical engineers or skilled employees performing services not generally available?
      `we agree to furnish those services, and those services only, at installation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As part of the contract of sale, does it agree to furnish such services, and such services only, to the vendee at the time of construction, erection or installation?
      `our business operations in Delaware are wholly interstate in character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its business operations within Delaware wholly interstate in character?
      `we are an insurance company doing business in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an insurance company doing business in Delaware?
      `we create, as borrower or lender, or acquire evidences of debt, mortgages or liens` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it create, as borrower or lender, or acquire, evidences of debt, mortgages or liens on real or personal property?
      `we secure or collect debts or enforce rights in property securing them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it secure or collect debts or enforce any rights in property securing them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foreign corporation excused from the qualification requirements of ss 371 and 372` IF
    `s 373(a) the foreign corporation is not required to comply with ss 371 and 372`
        (`s 373(a)(1) the foreign corporation is excused as a mail order or similar business` `we are in the mail order or a similar business` `we merely receive orders by mail or otherwise from letters, catalogs or other advertising` `we accept the orders outside Delaware` `we fill them with goods shipped into Delaware`)
        (`s 373(a)(2) the foreign corporation is excused as one soliciting orders through salespersons` `we employ salespersons to solicit orders in Delaware` `all orders are subject to approval at our offices outside Delaware` `all goods are shipped from outside Delaware to the vendee or the seller's agent for delivery` `we keep samples in Delaware` `our samples in Delaware are for display or advertising only` `no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock in Delaware`)
        (`s 373(a)(3) the foreign corporation is excused as a seller of machinery, plants or equipment` `we sell by contract consummated outside Delaware` `we agree to deliver into Delaware machinery, plants or equipment needing installation supervision` `we agree to furnish those services, and those services only, at installation`)
        (`s 373(a)(4) the foreign corporation is excused because its operations are wholly interstate` `our business operations in Delaware are wholly interstate in character`)
        (`s 373(a)(5) the foreign corporation is excused as an insurance company` `we are an insurance company doing business in Delaware`)
        (`s 373(a)(6) the foreign corporation is excused because it creates or acquires evidences of debt, mortgages or liens` `we create, as borrower or lender, or acquire evidences of debt, mortgages or liens`)
        (`s 373(a)(7) the foreign corporation is excused because it secures or collects debts or enforces rights in property securing them` `we secure or collect debts or enforce rights in property securing them`)

@export Does being excused under s 373 settle whether my foreign corporation can be served and sued in Delaware (s 373(b))?
GIVEN `s 373(a) excuses us from ss 371 and 372` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign corporation excused from ss 371 and 372 by s 373(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does being excused under s 373 settle whether my foreign corporation can be served and sued in Delaware` IF
    `s 373(b) the exception settles whether the foreign corporation is subject to service of process and suit in this State` `s 373(a) excuses us from ss 371 and 372`

-- s 374. The annual report.
@export Must my foreign corporation file an annual report with the Secretary of State (s 374)?
GIVEN `we are doing business in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign corporation doing business in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my foreign corporation file an annual report with the Secretary of State` IF
    `s 374 the foreign corporation must file an annual report with the Secretary of State` `we are doing business in Delaware`

@export By what date must my foreign corporation file its annual report for the year (s 374)?
GIVEN `the year of the report` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year is the report? (For example 2027.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my foreign corporation file its annual report for the year` IS
    `s 374 the last day to file the annual report for the year` `the year of the report`

@export Did my foreign corporation file its annual report in time (s 374)?
GIVEN `the year of the report` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year is the report? (For example 2027.)
      `the date we filed the report` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the report filed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my foreign corporation file its annual report in time` IF
    `s 374 the annual report was filed in time` `the year of the report` `the date we filed the report`

@export May I sign my foreign corporation's annual report (s 374)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `s 374 Person who signs the annual report` @desc What is your position: president, secretary, treasurer, another proper officer duly authorized to act, a director, an incorporator, or none of these?
      `it is an initial report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an initial report?
      `the board of directors has been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation's board of directors been elected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I sign my foreign corporation's annual report` IF
    `s 374 the person may sign the annual report` `my position` `it is an initial report` `the board of directors has been elected`

@export Is our annual report made and signed as the Law requires (s 374)?
GIVEN `it is on a form designated by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report made on a form designated by the Secretary of State?
      `the person who signed is one the Law allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who signed one the Law allows to sign it?
      `the signer's official title or position is designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the official title or position of the individual signing designated on the report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our annual report made and signed as the Law requires` IF
    `s 374 the report is made and signed as the section requires` `it is on a form designated by the Secretary of State` `the person who signed is one the Law allows` `the signer's official title or position is designated`

@export Is a signature on the certification attached to our report prima facie evidence that the signer may certify it (s 374)?
GIVEN `an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an individual's name signed on a certification attached to the corporate report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a signature on the certification attached to our report prima facie evidence that the signer may certify it` IF
    `s 374 the signature is prima facie evidence that the individual is authorized to certify the report` `an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to the report`

@export Does our annual report contain everything s 374 requires it to contain (s 374(1) to (4))?
GIVEN `it gives the location of the registered office with street, number, city and postal code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report give the location of the registered office in Delaware, including the street, number, city and postal code?
      `it gives the name of the agent for service of process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report give the name of the agent upon whom service of process against the corporation may be served?
      `it gives the location of the principal place of business with street, number, city and state or country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report give the location of the principal place of business, including the street, number, city, state or foreign country?
      `it gives the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report give the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date?
      `it gives the name and address of the officer who signs it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report give the name and address of the officer who signs it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our annual report contain everything s 374 requires it to contain` IF
        `s 374(1) the report contains the location of the registered office` `it gives the location of the registered office with street, number, city and postal code`
    AND `s 374(2) the report contains the name of the agent for service of process` `it gives the name of the agent for service of process`
    AND `s 374(3) the report contains the location of the principal place of business` `it gives the location of the principal place of business with street, number, city and state or country`
    AND `s 374(4) the report contains the names and addresses of the directors and of the signing officer` `it gives the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date` `it gives the name and address of the officer who signs it`

@export Am I guilty of perjury if I knowingly make a false statement in my foreign corporation's annual report (s 374)?
GIVEN `I am an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file an annual report with the Secretary of State?
      `I knowingly made a false statement in the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make a false statement in the report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of perjury if I knowingly make a false statement in my foreign corporation's annual report` IF
    `s 374 the officer or director is guilty of perjury` `I am an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file the report` `I knowingly made a false statement in the report`

